  "title": "DocumentParser",
  "description": "Validates untrusted document data of the current version. `parse` returns the data as the current document type, or throws. It runs after all migrations, so every document is checked in one place whatever its age. It validates data only: it builds no runtime objects and loads nothing. Check each field instead of casting; a TypeScript cast says nothing about what a file contains.",
